769298</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>The expert patient: A new approach to chronic disease management for the 21st century</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.dh.gov.uk/assetRoot/04/01/85/78/04018578.pdf"/></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rogers</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Damned by faint praise?</article-title><source>Chronic Illness</source><year>2006</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>262</fpage><lpage>264</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17212873</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1177/17423953060020040501</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Newbould</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Bury</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Lay-led self-management in chronic illness: a review of the evidence</article-title><source>Chronic Illness</source><year>2006</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>249</fpage><lpage>261</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17212872</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Swerissen</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Belfrage</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Weeks</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Jordan</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Walker</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Furler</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>McAvoy</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Carter</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Peterson</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A randomised control trial of a self-management program for people with a chronic illness from Vietnamese, Chinese, Italian and Greek backgrounds</article-title><source>Patient Educ Couns</source><year>2006</year><volume>64</volume><fpage>360</fpage><lpage>368</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16859871</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/j.pec.2006.04.003</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Walker</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Peterson</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Millen</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Walker C, Peterson C, Millen N, C M</surname></name></person-group><article-title>A proposal for a new model of chronic illness</article-title><source>Chronic illness: new perspectives and new directions</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name>Croydon, Vic.: Tertiary Press</publisher-name><fpage>17</fpage><lpage>35</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Blakeman</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Macdonald</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Bower</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Gately</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Chew-Graham</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A qualitative study of GPs' attitudes to self-management of chronic disease</article-title><source>Br J Gen Pract</source><year>2006</year><volume>56</volume><fpage>407</fpage><lpage>414</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16762121</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Penninx</surname><given-names>BW</given-names></name><name><surname>van Tilburg</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Deeg</surname><given-names>DJH</given-names></name><name><surname>Kriegsman</surname><given-names>DMW</given-names></name><name><surname>Boeke</surname><given-names>AJP</given-names></name><name><surname>van Eijk</surname><given-names>JTM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Direct and buffer effects of social support and personal coping resources in individuals with arthritis</article-title><source>Soc Sci Med</source><year>1997</year><volume>44</volume><fpage>393</fpage><lpage>402</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9004373</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0277-9536(96)00156-6</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Thoits</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hewitt</surname><given-names>LN</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Volunteer work and well-being</article-title><source>J Health Soc Behav</source><year>2001</year><volume>42</volume><fpage>115</fpage><lpage>131</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11467248</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2307/3090173</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Glasgow</surname><given-names>RE</given-names></name><name><surname>Toobert</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Gillette</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Psychosocial Barriers to Diabetes Self-Management and Quality of Life</article-title><source>Diabetes Spectr</source><year>2001</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>33</fpage><lpage>41</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2337/diaspect.14.1.33</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Young</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Furler</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Vale</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Walker</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Segal</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Dunning</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Best</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Blackberry</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Audehm</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Sulaiman</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Patient Engagement and Coaching for Health: The PEACH study &#x02013; A cluster randomised controlled trial using the telephone to coach people with type 2 diabetes to engage with their GPs to improve diabetes care: A study protocol</article-title><source>BMC Family Practice</source><year>2007</year><volume>8</volume><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17428318</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>2001 Census of Popuation and Housing</article-title><comment>http://www.censusdata.abs.gov.au/ABSNavigation/prenav/LocationSearch?locationLastSearchTerm=hume&#x00026;locationSearchTerm=hume&#x00026;newarea=LGA23270&#x00026;submitbutton=View+Community+Profiles+%3E&#x00026;mapdisplay=on&#x00026;collection=Census&#x00026;period=2006&#x00026;areacode=LGA23270&#x00026;geography=&#x00026;method=&#x00026;productlabel=&#x00026;producttype=Community+Profiles&#x00026;topic=&#x00026;navmapdisplayed=true&#x00026;javascript=true&#x00026;breadcrumb=  PL&#x00026;topholder=0&#x00026;leftholder=0&#x00026;currentaction=104&#x00026;action=401&#x00026;textversion=false&#x00026;subaction=1</comment></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>AIHW</collab></person-group><source>Diabetes related deaths 2001&#x02013;2003. AIHW Bulletin No. 32. AIHW Cat No. AUS 69</source><year>2005</year